---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getProjectById } from '../../../data/projects';

const project = getProjectById('disaster-recovery');

if (!project) {
  throw new Error('Disaster Recovery project data could not be found.');
}
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Homelab Disaster Recovery Platform"
  description="A practical disaster recovery platform using Restic backups, monitoring and recovery validation."
>

<section class="project-hero">
  <div class="container project-hero-grid">

    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Infrastructure Resilience Case Study</p>

      <h1>
        Disaster recovery designed for real-world failure.
      </h1>

      <p class="project-summary">
        A practical recovery platform built around automated Restic backups,
        infrastructure monitoring and repeatable rebuild procedures.
        The objective is not just protecting data, but proving that services
        can be recovered after failure.
      </p>

      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/projects">
          Back to projects
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>


    <aside class="project-facts">

      <p class="eyebrow">Project Overview</p>

      <dl>

        <div>
          <dt>Project type</dt>
          <dd>Disaster Recovery</dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt>Backup platform</dt>
          <dd>Restic</dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt>Infrastructure</dt>
          <dd>Linux / Docker / Raspberry Pi</dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt>Observability</dt>
          <dd>Prometheus + Grafana</dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt>Status</dt>
          <dd class="live-status">Active project</dd>
        </div>

      </dl>

    </aside>

  </div>
</section>


<section class="technology-strip">
<div class="container">

<ul class="tag-list">
{project.technologies.map((technology) =>
<li>{technology}</li>
)}
</ul>

</div>
</section>



<section class="section">

<div class="container content-grid">

<div class="section-heading">
<p class="eyebrow">The Challenge</p>
<h2>
Backups are only useful when recovery is proven.
</h2>
</div>


<div class="prose">

<p>
A growing homelab environment creates the same operational challenges
found in professional infrastructure. Hosts fail, storage can become
unavailable and configuration changes can introduce unexpected problems.
</p>

<p>
This project focuses on creating a predictable recovery process rather
than simply storing backup files. The aim is to rebuild services quickly,
safely and consistently.
</p>

</div>

</div>

</section>



<section class="section section-soft">

<div class="container">

<div class="section-heading">
<p class="eyebrow">Recovery Workflow</p>

<h2>
From failure to restored service.
</h2>

</div>


<div class="architecture">

<div class="architecture-item">
<span>01</span>
<strong>Backup</strong>
<p>
Restic captures important configuration, application data and system state.
</p>
</div>


<div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>


<div class="architecture-item">
<span>02</span>
<strong>Monitor</strong>
<p>
Prometheus metrics track backup success, age and repository health.
</p>
</div>


<div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>


<div class="architecture-item">
<span>03</span>
<strong>Recover</strong>
<p>
A replacement host can restore data and rebuild the environment.
</p>
</div>


<div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>


<div class="architecture-item">
<span>04</span>
<strong>Validate</strong>
<p>
Services are tested to confirm a successful recovery.
</p>
</div>

</div>

</div>

</section>



<section class="section">

<div class="container">

<div class="section-heading">

<p class="eyebrow">Engineering Implementation</p>

<h2>
Automated backup with operational visibility.
</h2>

</div>


<div class="grid capability-grid">


<article class="card">
<h3>Restic backups</h3>
<p>
Encrypted repositories provide point-in-time recovery with controlled
retention policies.
</p>
</article>


<article class="card">
<h3>Backup monitoring</h3>
<p>
Backup status, age and health are exposed as infrastructure metrics.
</p>
</article>


<article class="card">
<h3>Grafana visibility</h3>
<p>
Recovery readiness is displayed alongside the wider monitoring platform.
</p>
</article>


<article class="card">
<h3>DR testing</h3>
<p>
A dedicated Raspberry Pi 4 will be used to validate the complete recovery
process.
</p>
</article>


</div>

</div>

</section>



<section class="section section-soft">

<div class="container content-grid">

<div class="section-heading">

<p class="eyebrow">
Recovery Exercise
</p>

<h2>
Testing the plan, not just storing backups.
</h2>

</div>


<div class="prose">

<p>
The next phase is a full disaster recovery test using replacement hardware.
The exercise will measure recovery time, identify missing dependencies and
improve the rebuild documentation.
</p>

<p>
The final objective is a repeatable process that can recover the platform
after a complete host failure.
</p>

</div>

</div>

</section>



<section class="section">

<div class="container content-grid">

<div class="section-heading">
<p class="eyebrow">
Engineering Outcome
</p>

<h2>
Turning backups into resilience.
</h2>

</div>


<div class="prose">

<p>
This platform demonstrates that reliable infrastructure is not only about
running services successfully. It is about understanding how those services
can be restored when things go wrong.
</p>

</div>

</div>

</section>


</BaseLayout>



<style>

.project-hero {
padding:7rem 0 4rem;
}


.project-hero-grid {
display:grid;
grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.4fr) minmax(290px,.6fr);
gap:4rem;
}


h1 {
max-width:900px;
font-size:clamp(3rem,7vw,5.8rem);
line-height:.98;
letter-spacing:-.055em;
}


.project-summary {
max-width:760px;
color:var(--text-muted);
font-size:1.2rem;
}


.project-facts {
padding:1.75rem;
border:1px solid var(--border);
border-radius:var(--radius);
background:var(--surface);
}


.project-facts dl div {
padding:.8rem 0;
border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
}


.project-facts dt {
color:var(--text-muted);
font-size:.8rem;
text-transform:uppercase;
}


.project-facts dd {
margin:0;
font-weight:700;
}


.live-status {
color:#8ff0bc;
}


.architecture {
display:flex;
gap:.75rem;
}


.architecture-item {
flex:1;
padding:1.25rem;
border:1px solid var(--border);
border-radius:var(--radius);
background:var(--surface);
}


.architecture-item span {
color:var(--primary);
font-weight:800;
}


.architecture-item p {
color:var(--text-muted);
}


.architecture-arrow {
display:grid;
place-items:center;
color:var(--primary);
font-size:1.5rem;
}


@media(max-width:850px) {

.project-hero-grid {
grid-template-columns:1fr;
}

.architecture {
flex-direction:column;
}

.architecture-arrow {
transform:rotate(90deg);
}

}

</style>
